# Free Fire keymap 'HEY' exported from BlueStacks cfg (Downloads/com.dts.freefireth.cfg).
# Units: PERCENT of the landscape game view. Daemon scales % -> 0-32767
# touch range (rotation-independent: the MT frame maps 1:1 to the display).
# Format: TAP <HostKey> <X%> <Y%> | DPAD <X%> <Y%> <R%> <Up> <Dn> <Lf> <Rt> | FIRE <X%> <Y%>
# Hand-tuned notes: G favors Interact over the duplicate pickup tap; the
# Shift 'sprint tap' is dropped (sprint = full-deflection Dpad drag, not a tap).

DPAD 16.77 75.51 8.11 W S A D
# PAN look sens=2.93 (in-game sensitivity covers this; our drag is 1:1)
FIRE 79.24 78.98 # host LMB -> fire button (hold-capable)
TAP H 88.11 32.85 # Basic controls/Pick up items
# DUP key=G @92.99,33.99 (Basic controls/Pick up items) -- skipped, keeping Interact
TAP G 71.57 51.08 # Basic controls/Interact
TAP MouseRButton 96.21 54.05 # Combat/Use scope
TAP 1 86.00 18.87 # Combat/Change weapon
TAP 2 91.40 19.56 # Combat/Change weapon
TAP 3 98.09 19.68 # Combat/Change weapon
TAP 6 3.02 75.81 # Combat/Grenade
TAP R 98.38 4.16 # Combat/Reload
# SKIP Shift tap @16.73,43.55 (sprint = Dpad full deflection)
TAP space 97.55 70.79 # Movement/Jump (XKB keysym is lowercase)
TAP C 94.25 90.03 # Movement/Crouch
TAP Z 82.46 92.47 # Movement/Prone
# DUP key=G @71.37,62.54 (General/?) -- skipped, keeping Interact
TAP 5 3.12 62.90 # General/Healing
# TAB/backpack is intentionally unmapped: bare TAB is the capture toggle
# (compositor consumes it, the game never sees it). Open the backpack
# unlocked via Super+X peek, or tap its on-screen button.
TAP M 8.96 14.91 # General/Map
